# build-rpm.sh has no --help flag and no distro-validation guard.
# This file documents its stable observable interface.
#
# USAGE (from source):
#   build-rpm.sh [-release | <snapshot-suffix>]
#
# Without -release: treats $1 as a snapshot suffix appended to the package version.
# With -release:    builds a release RPM (RELEASE=1, no snapshot suffix).
# With no args:     auto-generates suffix from git timestamp + hash.
#
# The script emits the snapshot string it will use (stderr-like via warn()):
#   "*** using packageVersion .<suffix>"
# then runs rpmbuild — requires an RPM toolchain; no dry-run mode.
#
# The "using packageVersion" line is the only stable offline-testable output.
#
# VERIFIED with: bash build-rpm.sh badarg 2>&1 | grep "using packageVersion"
# Output: *** using packageVersion .badarg

*** using packageVersion
